# Preliminary snPATHO-seq Analysis

## Project overview

This repository contains preliminary computational workflows for processing and exploring single-nucleus RNA-sequencing data generated from GIST specimens. The scripts span Cell Ranger multi-sample processing, CellBender background removal, per-sample quality-control review, doublet-calling comparisons, sample-level PCA clustering and an alternative pooled scVI clustering/validation workflow. The sample names in the code are PATH01–PATH04; the repository itself does not include the count matrices, Cell Ranger configuration CSVs, intermediate AnnData objects, environment lockfiles or result files.

The scientific purpose is to characterise the cellular composition of GIST specimens and create analysis outputs that can support later tumour-microenvironment interpretation. The code documents computational procedures and candidate marker visualisation. It does not by itself establish cell identities, subtype effects, treatment response, or successful completion of any analysis. In particular, a UMAP or cluster-marker output is an exploratory representation requiring biological review and validation.

The repository is developmental and branch-oriented. Some branch names suggest successive stages, but the Git history is not a single linear, executable pipeline: the `main` tip is identical to `4_Sample_Integration`, whose committed tree contains only the placeholder README. The raw-processing, QC, doublet, sample-level clustering and pooled clustering workflows are on separate branch tips. The `4_Sample_Integration` branch contains no integration implementation, while the pooled clustering scripts require external `merged_scVI_25PCs.h5ad` and `merged_scVI_30PCs.h5ad` objects. Treat the branch table and branch README files as the authoritative inventory of what is actually present.

